56":"sha256:c5b55b2b4dcae7061c88dae56b0136d206c111a8ff0a37b16e757ffcd9290341","file":"preprints/Uniform-Bi-Holder-Transport-from-Weak-MTW-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":32,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2d97ecf6c3fef8e1607563f95c1b16406551ba219a96889c3c063fb215978179","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Uniform-Bi-Holder-Transport-from-Weak-MTW-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c5b55b2b4dcae7061c88dae56b0136d206c111a8ff0a37b16e757ffcd9290341","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Uniform-Bi-Holder-Transport-from-Weak-MTW-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L32"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFix $(M,g)$ as above and $0<\\lambda\\leq\\Lambda<\\infty$ for which the\nfollowing density class is nonempty. There are\n$\\alpha\\in(0,1]$ and $C<\\infty$, depending only on\n$(M,g),\\lambda,\\Lambda$, such that the following holds for every pair\nof measurable densities satisfying\n\\[\n \\int_M\\rho_i\\,d\\vol=1,\\qquad\n \\lambda\\leq\\rho_i\\leq\\Lambda\\quad\\vol\\text{-almost everywhere},\n \\qquad i=0,1.\n\\]\nThe almost-everywhere unique optimal map from $\\rho_0\\vol$ to\n$\\rho_1\\vol$ for the cost $c$ has a homeomorphic representative\n$\\widetilde T:M\\to M$, and\n\\[\n d(\\widetilde T(x),\\widetilde T(x'))\\leq C d(x,x')^\\alpha,\n \\qquad\n d(\\widetilde T^{-1}(y),\\widetilde T^{-1}(y'))\n       \\leq C d(y,y')^\\alpha\n\\]\nfor all $x,x',y,y'\\in M$."}
